{"meta":{"format_version":"4.10","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"cannon_bronze","model_identifier":"cannon_bronze","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"## cannon_bronze\n\nField cannon, bronze (E1).\n\n- Cubes: 52 (14 rotated). Texture 256x128, 1 px per unit, embedded.\n- Bounds at rest: x -14.0..14.0, y 0.0..39.0, z -32.1..34.0 (size 28.0 x 39.0 x 66.1 u = 79 x 110 x 186 cm).\nField cannon: about 1.8 m long with the trail (66 u), barrel 1.2 m, wheels 1.1 m. Short, thick bronze barrel (1.2 m = 42.7 u, warm golden-brown) with a flared cast muzzle ring, a heavier reinforce with two lion-face mouldings near the breech, base ring and cascabel knob, on an oak two-wheeled carriage with iron straps and cap-squares, a sloping trail with an iron shoe and lunette, a team-colour stripe along the trail, 1.1 m spoked wheels with iron tyres, and a sponge bucket hanging from the trail.\nHauled field gun, faces -Z (muzzle forward), stands on y = 0 on its wheels and trail shoe.\n\n**Hit box:** one box 28 x 39 x 66 u (w x h x d), centred x = 0, z = 1, from y = 0.\n\n**Bones:** `root` > `carriage` (pivot at the trail shoe, so the fire hop rocks on the trail) > `barrel` (pivot at the trunnions, pitch = elevation; the game may set it directly to aim) > `fx_muzzle` (empty, at the muzzle mouth: spawn flash/smoke/ball here), `wheel_r`, `wheel_l` (pivots on the axle), `bucket` (sponge bucket).\n\n**Slots:** `slot_hitch` at the trail-end lunette (the limber or the animal's draw-bar hooks here; guns are towed trail-first), `slot_crew_1` = loader/rammer, standing 40 u in front of the muzzle, slightly right, facing +Z back toward the muzzle (the dwarf crew's `ram` key reaches ~40 u forward and ~20 u up), `slot_crew_2` = gunner beside the trail on the left, facing -Z. Crew slots sit on the ground (y = 0) and are children of `root` so they do not jump with the gun.\n\n**Move speed:** `move` is designed for 35.6 u/s (1.0 m/s, ox/horse walk): the wheels make one turn per 3.44 s (circumference 122.5 u). `move` rolls the wheels for travel toward -Z (muzzle first, crew man-handling it); `move_towed` rolls them the other way for travel toward +Z (trail first behind the animal). Scale the clip speed for other speeds.\n\n**Key times:** `fire` key 0.08 s (the flash: spawn the ball at `fx_muzzle`); the gun jumps back 10.7 u (30 cm) by 0.4 s with a hop and wheel roll, settles, and the crew run it back into battery from 1.5 s to 2.4 s. `reload` key 2.4 s (loaded; the barrel is levelled for loading 0.5-2.4 s, then relaid). `aim` loops an elevation sweep. `damaged` 0.7 s shudder with a wobbling left wheel. `destroyed` holds: the right wheel breaks off and falls flat, the carriage drops onto its broken side, the barrel tips off its trunnions.\n\n**Props:** rammer and powder ladle for the crew are separate files in `cannon_rammer/`.\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop |\n|---|---|---|\n| `idle` | 4 | loop |\n| `move` | 3.442 | loop |\n| `move_towed` | 3.442 | loop |\n| `fire` | 2.4 | once |\n| `reload` | 3 | once |\n| `aim` | 3 | loop |\n| `damaged` | 0.7 | once |\n| `destroyed` | 1.6 | hold |\n"},"description":"## cannon_bronze\n\nField cannon, bronze (E1).\n\n- Cubes: 52 (14 rotated). Texture 256x128, 1 px per unit, embedded.\n- Bounds at rest: x -14.0..14.0, y 0.0..39.0, z -32.1..34.0 (size 28.0 x 39.0 x 66.1 u = 79 x 110 x 186 cm).\nField cannon: about 1.8 m long with the trail (66 u), barrel 1.2 m, wheels 1.1 m. Short, thick bronze barrel (1.2 m = 42.7 u, warm golden-brown) with a flared cast muzzle ring, a heavier reinforce with two lion-face mouldings near the breech, base ring and cascabel knob, on an oak two-wheeled carriage with iron straps and cap-squares, a sloping trail with an iron shoe and lunette, a team-colour stripe along the trail, 1.1 m spoked wheels with iron tyres, and a sponge bucket hanging from the trail.\nHauled field gun, faces -Z (muzzle forward), stands on y = 0 on its wheels and trail shoe.\n\n**Hit box:** one box 28 x 39 x 66 u (w x h x d), centred x = 0, z = 1, from y = 0.\n\n**Bones:** `root` > `carriage` (pivot at the trail shoe, so the fire hop rocks on the trail) > `barrel` (pivot at the trunnions, pitch = elevation; the game may set it directly to aim) > `fx_muzzle` (empty, at the muzzle mouth: spawn flash/smoke/ball here), `wheel_r`, `wheel_l` (pivots on the axle), `bucket` (sponge bucket).\n\n**Slots:** `slot_hitch` at the trail-end lunette (the limber or the animal's draw-bar hooks here; guns are towed trail-first), `slot_crew_1` = loader/rammer, standing 40 u in front of the muzzle, slightly right, facing +Z back toward the muzzle (the dwarf crew's `ram` key reaches ~40 u forward and ~20 u up), `slot_crew_2` = gunner beside the trail on the left, facing -Z. Crew slots sit on the ground (y = 0) and are children of `root` so they do not jump with the gun.\n\n**Move speed:** `move` is designed for 35.6 u/s (1.0 m/s, ox/horse walk): the wheels make one turn per 3.44 s (circumference 122.5 u). `move` rolls the wheels for travel toward -Z (muzzle first, crew man-handling it); `move_towed` rolls them the other way for travel toward +Z (trail first behind the animal). Scale the clip speed for other speeds.\n\n**Key times:** `fire` key 0.08 s (the flash: spawn the ball at `fx_muzzle`); the gun jumps back 10.7 u (30 cm) by 0.4 s with a hop and wheel roll, settles, and the crew run it back into battery from 1.5 s to 2.4 s. `reload` key 2.4 s (loaded; the barrel is levelled for loading 0.5-2.4 s, then relaid). `aim` loops an elevation sweep. `damaged` 0.7 s shudder with a wobbling left wheel. `destroyed` holds: the right wheel breaks off and falls flat, the carriage drops onto its broken side, the barrel tips off its trunnions.\n\n**Props:** rammer and powder ladle for the crew are separate files in `cannon_rammer/`.\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop |\n|---|---|---|\n| `idle` | 4 | loop |\n| `move` | 3.442 | loop |\n| `move_towed` | 3.442 | loop |\n| `fire` | 2.4 | once |\n| `reload` | 3 | once |\n| `aim` | 3 | loop |\n| `damaged` | 0.7 | once |\n| `destroyed` | 1.6 | hold |\n","resolution":{"width":256,"height":128},"elements":[{"name":"cheek_r","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"light_emission":0,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[5.5,15.0,-17.0],"to":[7.5,26.0,1.0],"autouv":0,"color":0,"inflate":0.0,"origin":[0.0,0.0,32.0],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[98,39,100.0,50.0],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[26,39,44.0,50.0],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[100,39,102.0,50.0],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[44,39,62.0,50.0],"texture":0},"up":{"uv":[118,0,120.0,18.0],"texture":0},"down":{"uv":[120,0,122.0,18.0],"texture":0}},"type":"cube","uuid":"8bb8e5f0-2595-5a1c-b96c-ffe08410ef73"},{"name":"capsquare_r","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"light_emission":0,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[5.25,25.5,-10.75],"to":[7.75,26.5,-7.25],"autouv":0,"color":0,"inflate":0.0,"origin":[0.0,0.0,32.0],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[220,76,222.5,77.0],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[204,76,207.5,77.0],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[223,76,225.5,77.0],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[208,76,211.5,77.0],"texture":0},"up":{"uv":[133,62,135.5,65.5],"texture":0},"down":{"uv":[136,62,138.5,65.5],"texture":0}},"type":"cube","uuid":"d070b843-fa24-5708-8090-bfc08fb65f91"},{"name":"cheek_l","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"light_emission":0,"render_order":"default","allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[-7.5,15.0,-17.0],"to":[-5.5,26.0,1.0],"autouv":0,"color":0,"inflate":0.0,"origin":[0.0,0.0,32.0],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[102,39,104.0,50.0],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[62,39,80.0,50.0],"texture":0},"south":{"uv":[104,39,106.0,50.0],"texture":0},"west":{"uv":[80,39,98.0,50.0],"texture":0},"up":{"uv":[122,0,124.0,18.0],"texture":0},"down":{"uv":[124,0,126.0,18.0],"texture":0}},"type":"cube","uuid":"b1ca5db9-9b01-5b03-b73c-5ffbddab3ce3"},{"